%[text] %[text:anchor:T_DEF03274] # Vector Arithmetic
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_E8C62B23] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_DED66B9A] ### [VectorBasics.m](file:./Scripts/VectorBasics.m) 
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,520],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Decompose a vector v into a component v\_x in the x direction and v\_y in the y direction](text:image:1106) | <p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Relate the components of a vector to its visualization in 2- and 3-dimensions</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Compute the magnitude of a vector in 2- and 3-dimensions</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Compute the orientation of a vector in 2-dimensions</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Discuss the meaning of the magnitude of an accelerometer reading</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Relate the pitch of a cell phone to accelerometer readings</p><p></p> |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_B5427BEB] ### [VectorArithmetic.m](file:./Scripts/VectorArithmetic.m) 
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,522],"ignoreHeader":true}
%[text] |  | **In this script, students will...** |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![A cell phone with a normal vector pointing straight out from the screen and an acceleration vector pointing straight up against gravity with the cell phone flat on a surface, at a 30 degree angle, at a 70 degree angle, and at right angles to the surface](text:image:3931) | <p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Add and subtract vectors</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Compute scalar, dot, and cross products of vectors</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Relate arithmetic vector operations to visual representations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Identify the physical meaning of the results of arithmetic vector operations</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"\bullet"} Apply vector arithmetic to compute the yaw of a cell phone</p><p></p> |
%[text:table]
